# Patch files must check out byte-for-byte identical to what's committed:
# git apply is sensitive to exact line endings, and a plain checkout on a
# machine/runner with core.autocrlf=true (e.g. GitHub's windows-latest
# runners) converts LF -> CRLF for anything git considers "text", which
# corrupts the diff (confirmed 2026-08-06: reproduced GitHub Actions'
# "error: corrupt patch at line 45" locally just by CRLF-converting the
# committed patch and nothing else). Marking these -text disables that
# conversion entirely for these paths, in both directions.
patches/*.patch -text
